# HASTABAZAAR SELLER MARKETPLACE AGREEMENT

> **Preparation status — 16 September 2026:** Hasta Bazaar is the name accepted for registration, as reported by the founder. Incorporation is pending. Hastabazaar is the marketplace brand. The exact registered name and suffix, certificate, PAN/VAT details, address and e-commerce listing remain to be verified. This draft does not assert that the proposed company already exists or bind it before lawful execution. Effective date remains pending. Commercial launch requires completed applicable registrations and operational approval.

**DRAFT FOR LEGAL AND COMMERCIAL REVIEW — NOT FOR EXECUTION**

**Version:** Draft 3.0  
**Effective Date:** [DD/MM/YYYY]  
**Last Updated:** 16/09/2026

This Seller Marketplace Agreement (the **“Agreement”**) governs the contractual relationship between:

**Hasta Bazaar [exact registered suffix and legal form pending]**, the proposed Nepalese entity identified in the preparation notice above, which may execute this Agreement only after lawful establishment and completion of required registrations, operating the electronic marketplace under the brand name **“Hastabazaar”**, having its registered office at [REGISTERED ADDRESS], Company/Firm Registration No. [●], PAN/VAT No. [●], and Electronic-Commerce Listing No. [●] (**“Hastabazaar,” “Platform,” “we,” “us,” or “our”**);

and

the individual proprietor, firm, company, cooperative, enterprise, industry, or other legally eligible and registered business person identified in **Schedule 1** and the corresponding Seller Account (**“Seller” or “you”**).

Hastabazaar and the Seller are individually a **“Party”** and collectively the **“Parties.”**

## ELECTRONIC ACCEPTANCE

This Agreement may be entered into electronically. By actively selecting an unticked **“I Agree”** checkbox or using another legally valid electronic acceptance method presented by Hastabazaar, completing Seller verification, and activating the Seller Account, the Seller confirms that:

1. the Seller has received or can download this Agreement and the Platform Policies;
2. the Seller has read, understood, and agreed to be legally bound by them;
3. the individual accepting the Agreement is legally competent and authorized to bind the Seller; and
4. the Seller information contained in Schedule 1 or the acceptance record is complete and accurate.

Hastabazaar may maintain an electronic acceptance record containing the Seller’s verified identity, authorized representative, date and time of acceptance, Agreement version, accepted Platform Policy versions, and other lawful authentication information. Hastabazaar shall provide the Seller with access to a downloadable copy of the accepted version.

Where applicable law requires a different or additional form of execution or authentication, that requirement shall prevail.

## 1. DEFINITIONS AND INTERPRETATION

### 1.1 Definitions

In this Agreement:

**“Affected Product Value”** means the price payable for the delayed Order line after Seller-funded discounts and before any Hastabazaar-funded discount that does not reduce Seller proceeds, less the tax attributable to that line. Delivery, tips, payment-processing charges and unrelated items are excluded. Tax embedded in a tax-inclusive price shall be backed out using the applicable tax treatment. Tax records determine the base; a Customer promotion funded by Hastabazaar does not reduce it.

**“Applicable Law”** means all laws, regulations, directives, orders, notices, licence conditions, and binding regulatory requirements applicable in Nepal, including the Electronic Commerce (E-Commerce) Act, 2081, the Electronic Transactions Act, 2063, the Consumer Protection Act, 2075, the Individual Privacy Act, 2075, applicable tax and payment laws, and rules or directives issued under them, as amended or replaced.

**“Business Day”** means a day on which commercial banks are generally open for business in Kathmandu, Nepal, excluding public holidays.

**“Customer”** means a buyer or consumer who purchases or begins the process of purchasing a Product through the Platform.

**“Delayed Order”** means an accepted Order or Order line that the Seller fails to make ready and hand over within the applicable Seller Processing Deadline, excluding a delay covered by Clause 13.8.

**“Made-to-Order Product”** means a Product that is produced or completed after an Order is accepted and is clearly identified as made to order before purchase.

**“Order”** means a Customer request to purchase one or more Products through the Platform.

**“Platform Policies”** means the policies identified in Schedule 3, as validly amended under Clause 29.

**“Product”** means any good offered, listed, sold, or proposed to be sold by the Seller through the Platform.

**“Ready-to-Ship Product”** means a Product represented as existing, available, and capable of dispatch within the displayed processing period.

**“Seller Account”** means the Seller’s account, dashboard, or Seller Centre used to access marketplace services.

**“Seller-Fault”** means an act or omission attributable to the Seller, including inaccurate listing information, defective or non-conforming Products, insufficient inventory, inadequate packaging, delay within the Seller’s control, infringement, illegality, or breach of this Agreement.

**“Seller Processing Deadline”** means the date and time by which the Seller must make an accepted Order ready and complete the required handover to Hastabazaar or the approved carrier, as shown in the accepted Order, listing, or applicable service-level policy.

**“Settlement Amount”** means the amount payable to the Seller for completed Orders after applying the Product price, Seller-funded discounts, commissions, taxes required to be withheld, refunds, authorized charges, reserves, and other deductions permitted by this Agreement.

### 1.2 Interpretation

Headings are for convenience only. The words “including” and “includes” mean “including without limitation.” Singular words include the plural and vice versa where the context permits. A reference to a law includes its amendments, replacements, and subordinate instruments.

### 1.3 Priority

If documents conflict, the following order applies unless mandatory law requires otherwise:

1. Applicable Law;
2. an Order-specific term expressly accepted by the Seller and Customer;
3. this Agreement;
4. the Seller Fee Schedule;
5. the other Platform Policies.

## 2. PURPOSE AND NATURE OF THE MARKETPLACE

### 2.1

Hastabazaar operates an intermediary electronic marketplace enabling eligible sellers, makers, artisans, creators, producers, and businesses to display, market, and sell lawful Products through Hastabazaar’s website, mobile application, social-commerce channels, and related electronic systems.

### 2.2

Unless a Product is expressly identified as sold directly by Hastabazaar, the Seller is the seller and supplier of that Product, and the sale contract is between the Seller and the Customer.

### 2.3

Hastabazaar may provide or facilitate marketplace access, product listing, order processing, payment collection and settlement, customer support, promotions, delivery coordination, returns, refunds, Seller analytics, photography, catalogue support, Seller training, and related services.

### 2.4 Limited Authority

The Seller authorizes Hastabazaar, solely as necessary to operate the marketplace, to:

1. display and promote approved listings;
2. communicate Order and Customer-service information;
3. collect Customer payments on the Seller’s behalf through legally approved payment channels;
4. issue or facilitate receipts and invoices as allocated under this Agreement;
5. process refunds, cancellations, chargebacks, and adjustments authorized by this Agreement or required by law;
6. coordinate fulfilment, delivery, returns, and complaints; and
7. perform the other expressly described marketplace functions.

Hastabazaar has no authority to bind the Seller for unrelated purposes.

### 2.5

Listing, temporary storage, pickup, transport, or return of a Product does not by itself transfer Product ownership to Hastabazaar.

### 2.6 Mandatory Responsibilities

The allocation of responsibilities in this Agreement does not exclude or reduce any non-waivable obligation of Hastabazaar, the Seller, a carrier, or another person under Applicable Law. Hastabazaar shall not refuse to register, investigate, or address a Customer complaint solely because Hastabazaar did not manufacture, import, or supply the Product.

### 2.7 Independent Businesses

Except for the limited authority expressly granted in Clause 2.4, the Parties are independent contracting businesses. Nothing creates employment, partnership, joint venture, franchise, or general agency between them.

## 3. SELLER ELIGIBILITY AND VERIFICATION

### 3.1

Before any Product is activated for commercial sale, the Seller shall provide, as applicable:

1. a valid business, firm, industry, enterprise, company, cooperative, or other legally applicable registration certificate;
2. a valid Business PAN and VAT registration where required;
3. a citizenship certificate, National ID, passport, or other legally acceptable identity document of the proprietor or authorized representative;
4. registered, operating, pickup, and return addresses;
5. current telephone number and email address;
6. bank or approved settlement-account information in the Seller’s lawful name;
7. return, refund, customer-service, and grievance contact information;
8. Product-specific licences, approvals, test reports, or certificates required by law;
9. authorization documents for the representative accepting this Agreement; and
10. additional risk-based KYC or verification information reasonably required for fraud prevention, regulatory compliance, payment processing, or Customer protection.

### 3.2 Individual Makers

An individual maker is not required to incorporate a private limited company merely to become a Seller. The maker must, however, operate through a form legally eligible for the activity—such as a registered sole proprietorship, firm, cottage or small industry, cooperative, enterprise, or company—and maintain the business and tax registrations required by Applicable Law.

### 3.3 Formalization Pending

Hastabazaar may allow an unregistered maker to submit a preliminary application or participate in a formalization or training programme. No Product shall be activated for commercial sale until the Seller satisfies Hastabazaar’s legal verification requirements.

### 3.4 Continuing Verification

The Seller shall keep all verification information current, notify Hastabazaar within forty-eight hours of any material change, and immediately notify Hastabazaar of any expiry, cancellation, suspension, or restriction affecting its authority to operate or sell a Product.

### 3.5

Hastabazaar may verify information through issuing authorities, lawful databases, payment providers, and reasonable inspection. Verification does not transfer the Seller’s legal responsibility to Hastabazaar.

## 4. SELLER ACCOUNT AND SECURITY

### 4.1

The Seller shall maintain accurate information and restrict account access to authorized users.

### 4.2

The Seller is responsible for reasonable security of passwords, OTPs, devices, login credentials, and authorized-user accounts and shall not share credentials with unauthorized persons.

### 4.3

The Seller shall notify Hastabazaar immediately after discovering suspected unauthorized access, credential compromise, or fraudulent activity.

### 4.4

The Seller is responsible for activity performed through credentials issued to its authorized users, except to the extent caused by Hastabazaar’s security failure or occurring after timely notice and reasonable opportunity for Hastabazaar to restrict access.

### 4.5

Hastabazaar may temporarily restrict access where reasonably necessary for security, fraud prevention, investigation, regulatory compliance, or Customer protection, subject to Clause 26.

## 5. SELLER REPRESENTATIONS AND WARRANTIES

The Seller represents and warrants throughout the term that:

1. it is legally eligible and properly registered to conduct the represented business;
2. all information and documents supplied are accurate, current, complete, and not misleading;
3. it owns or has lawful authority to sell and deliver every listed Product;
4. each Product complies with Applicable Law, safety requirements, labelling standards, and mandatory quality standards;
5. all necessary Product licences and regulatory approvals have been obtained and remain valid;
6. Products are not stolen, counterfeit, prohibited, unlawfully sourced, or illegally imported;
7. Products and listing content do not infringe intellectual-property, privacy, publicity, cultural-heritage, or other third-party rights;
8. it will comply with consumer, tax, invoicing, labelling, safety, quality, e-commerce, anti-corruption, and fair-trading obligations;
9. it will not offer an unsafe Product or conceal a known defect or recall; and
10. it has authority to grant the licences and indemnities contained in this Agreement.

## 6. HANDMADE AND MAKER AUTHENTICITY

### 6.1 Fundamental Standard

Truthful authenticity and origin claims are fundamental conditions of participation in Hastabazaar.

### 6.2

If a Product is described as handmade, handcrafted, artisan-made, maker-made, locally made, traditional, heritage, original, sustainable, made in Nepal, or personally made by the Seller, the Seller guarantees that the claim is accurate, not misleading, and capable of verification.

### 6.3 Production Method

The Seller shall accurately identify whether a Product is:

1. entirely handmade;
2. handmade using tools or machinery;
3. hand-assembled;
4. designed by the Seller and produced by a disclosed third-party producer;
5. customized or finished by the Seller;
6. commercially manufactured; or
7. sourced or resold from another producer.

Material outsourced production steps and the actual producer shall be disclosed where necessary to prevent a misleading authenticity claim.

### 6.4 Evidence

Hastabazaar may request proportionate evidence, including production or workshop photographs, process videos, raw-material records, maker identity, sourcing records, invoices, samples, or inspection access. Confidential production information shall be handled under Clause 23.

### 6.5 Enforcement

A serious or repeated authenticity violation may result in listing removal, badge removal, refund, suspension, termination, and recovery of reasonable amounts under Clauses 26 and 28. Hastabazaar shall provide the Seller with the basis of the decision and an opportunity to respond, except where an immediate restriction is reasonably required for fraud, illegality, evidence preservation, or Customer protection.

## 7. VERIFIED SELLER OR MAKER STATUS

### 7.1

Hastabazaar may establish designations such as Verified Seller, Verified Maker, or Heritage Artisan using published eligibility criteria.

### 7.2

A designation means only that the Seller satisfied Hastabazaar’s stated process as of the verification date. It is not government certification unless expressly identified as such.

### 7.3

Hastabazaar may suspend or withdraw a designation if the Seller no longer satisfies the criteria, after notice and review where reasonably practicable.

### 7.4

The Seller shall not reproduce, alter, or display a verification badge outside authorized Platform use without written permission.

## 8. PRODUCT LISTINGS AND DISCLOSURES

### 8.1

The Seller shall provide complete, truthful, current, and understandable information for every Product, including where applicable:

1. Product name, nature, description, specifications, design, shape, and clear photographs;
2. brand or trademark;
3. materials, composition, ingredients, underlying elements, quantity, dimensions, and weight;
4. colour and reasonably expected handmade variations;
5. actual producer, manufacturer, maker, or service provider;
6. Product origin and, for imported Products, country of production or processing;
7. final selling price including applicable tax;
8. separately disclosed delivery or transfer charges and any other legally permitted charge;
9. available quantity or made-to-order status;
10. processing deadline and expected delivery date or period;
11. accepted payment methods;
12. customization choices and confirmation requirements;
13. warranty or guarantee period and conditions;
14. post-sale conditions and instructions;
15. cancellation availability before dispatch;
16. return, exchange, and refund eligibility and conditions;
17. precautions, safe-use instructions, allergens, age restrictions, and warnings;
18. manufacturing date, batch number, expiry or consumption date, and legally required labels;
19. principal Order terms in language reasonably understandable to the intended Customer;
20. Customer review, rating, complaint, feedback, and grievance mechanism; and
21. any additional information reasonably required by Hastabazaar or Applicable Law.

### 8.2 Accuracy

The Product delivered must materially correspond with the listing and confirmed Order. The Seller shall promptly correct inaccuracies and pause a listing if a material correction cannot immediately be made.

### 8.3 Prohibited Listing Practices

The Seller shall not use fake or materially altered photographs, deceptive descriptions, hidden charges, artificially inflated reference prices or discounts, false scarcity, undisclosed commercial manufacture, misleading origin or sustainability claims, keyword manipulation, or another unfair practice.

### 8.4 Handmade Variation

Reasonable variation in texture, shade, grain, stitching, pattern, shape, or dimension may occur where inherent in handmade production and clearly disclosed before purchase. Handmade variation does not excuse a material defect, unsafe Product, failure to follow confirmed customization, or material difference from the listing.

### 8.5 Listing Review

Hastabazaar may edit formatting, request clarification, reject, pause, or remove a listing for quality, legal, safety, authenticity, intellectual-property, or policy reasons. Hastabazaar shall not make a substantive Product claim without Seller approval unless necessary to correct an obvious error or comply with law.

## 9. PROHIBITED AND RESTRICTED PRODUCTS

### 9.1

The Seller shall not list or sell:

1. goods or services prohibited from electronic sale by law or government notice;
2. stolen or counterfeit Products;
3. Products infringing third-party rights;
4. illegal wildlife, forestry, archaeological, cultural-heritage, or environmental products;
5. controlled or restricted goods without required authorization;
6. illegal drugs, substances, weapons, explosives, or dangerous Products prohibited for public sale;
7. recalled, expired, adulterated, unsafe, or materially mislabelled Products;
8. illegally imported or unlawfully sourced Products;
9. Products prohibited by the Prohibited Products Policy; or
10. Products for which the Seller lacks the required licence or authority.

### 9.2

Hastabazaar may immediately remove or suspend such a listing and may notify or cooperate with competent authorities where required or legally permitted.

### 9.3 Product Safety and Recall

The Seller shall immediately notify Hastabazaar of a known or suspected safety issue, regulatory investigation, recall, or mandatory warning and shall cooperate in stopping sales, identifying affected Orders, notifying Customers, refunding or replacing Products, and conducting a lawful recall. Costs shall be allocated according to fault and Applicable Law.

## 10. PRICING, TAXES, AND PROMOTIONS

### 10.1

The Seller determines its Product price, subject to Applicable Law and Platform rules. The price shown to the Customer must include applicable tax, while delivery charges and other legally permitted charges must be separately and clearly disclosed before Order confirmation.

### 10.2

The Seller shall not engage in deceptive pricing, hidden fees, price manipulation, or misleading discount claims.

### 10.3 Hastabazaar-Funded Promotions

Hastabazaar may fund a promotion at its own cost without reducing the Seller’s agreed Settlement Amount unless the Seller accepts different written campaign terms.

### 10.4 Seller-Funded Promotions

A promotion reducing the Seller’s proceeds requires the Seller’s prior participation or acceptance of clearly disclosed campaign terms.

### 10.5 Sponsored Placement

Paid placement or other preferential Seller treatment shall be clearly identified to Customers. Performance-based ranking shall use disclosed objective factors consistently and remain subject to Applicable Law.

### 10.6 No General Price Parity

Hastabazaar shall not require the Listed Price to be identical to prices on unrelated sales channels unless the Seller separately accepts a lawful campaign or programme containing that condition.

## 11. ORDERS AND CONTRACT FORMATION

### 11.1

A listing is an invitation for Customers to submit an Order unless the listing expressly states otherwise.

### 11.2

Unless Applicable Law establishes an earlier formation time, an Order is accepted when the Platform sends the confirmation following Seller acceptance or an automated method expressly enabled by the Seller. Seller supply obligations and Hasta Bazaar’s separate marketplace and statutory obligations remain enforceable according to law.

### 11.3

Payment authorization or receipt before Order confirmation does not by itself require acceptance where rejection is legally permitted. If an Order is not accepted or is lawfully cancelled, the Customer shall receive the required refund within the period prescribed by Applicable Law.

### 11.4

The Seller shall fulfil accepted Orders according to the listing, confirmed customization, Seller Processing Deadline, Customer instructions accepted through the Platform, and Platform Policies.

### 11.5

The Seller shall not cancel an accepted Order without a legitimate and documented reason. Repeated Seller-caused cancellation may affect Seller Performance under Clause 26.

### 11.6

Hastabazaar may reject or cancel an Order where reasonably necessary because of fraud, illegality, safety, unavailability, regulatory requirements, material listing or pricing error, Customer request, or another legitimate reason. Hastabazaar shall communicate the reason where lawful and ensure prompt refund of any amount due.

### 11.7

Order modifications after acceptance require agreement through the Platform by the affected parties, including any revised price and deadline.

## 12. PRODUCT FULFILMENT CATEGORIES

### 12.1 Ready-to-Ship

For a Ready-to-Ship Product, the Seller confirms that it physically exists, is available for sale, matches the listing, can be safely packaged, and can be handed over within the displayed processing period.

### 12.2 Made to Order

A Product requiring production after acceptance shall be clearly marked Made to Order with a realistic production period. The disclosed made-to-order deadline, rather than an ordinary ready-stock deadline, shall apply.

### 12.3 Customized or Personalized Products

For an engraved, personalized, custom-sized, custom-coloured, custom-designed, or otherwise customized Product:

1. Customer requirements must be confirmed through the Platform;
2. the Seller is responsible for following the confirmed requirements;
3. special cancellation or return restrictions apply only if lawful and clearly disclosed before purchase; and
4. no restriction excludes remedies for defects, unsafe Products, false descriptions, or failure to follow confirmed instructions.

### 12.4 Delay Notice

The Seller shall notify Hastabazaar through the designated system as soon as it becomes aware of a likely material delay and request any extension before the Seller Processing Deadline. Notice does not automatically excuse the delay.

## 13. PROCESSING TIME AND AUTOMATIC 20% DELAY PENALTY

### 13.1 Accurate Deadlines

The Seller shall declare realistic production, processing, and handover times and maintain sufficient operational capacity for accepted Orders.

### 13.2 Timely Handover

Except for an exclusion under Clause 13.8, the Seller shall complete packaging and documented handover to Hastabazaar or the approved carrier no later than the Seller Processing Deadline.

### 13.3 Automatic Penalty

**Hastabazaar does impose an automatic twenty percent (20%) delayed-fulfilment penalty on a Delayed Order, as a provisional contractual assessment subject to Clauses 13.4–13.8 and Applicable Law.**

> **Provisional assessment = 20% × Affected Product Value**

Assessment applies once per delayed Order line and does not compound. Final recovery is limited to the reasonable amount legally recoverable and shall not exceed that assessment. An automatic system event does not by itself prove liability.

### 13.4 Purpose and Basis

The rate is intended to address reasonably foreseeable delay-related support, rescheduling, administration and other recoverable impact. The Parties do not declare it reasonable merely by signing. Hasta Bazaar shall maintain a documented basis for the proposed rate, assess causation and proportionality, and reduce or waive recovery where the facts or Applicable Law require. It is not a government fine or Customer charge. Review of this clause under Nepal’s contractual compensation rules is required before activation.

### 13.5 Standard Assessment Procedure

1. Record the accepted deadline, time zone, delayed lines and approved extensions.
2. Check readiness records, pickup availability, handover evidence and any excluded cause.
3. Calculate a provisional 20% assessment using the tax-exclusive base and place it in pending status.
4. Notify the Seller of the evidence, base, calculation, grounds, response route and deadline.
5. Allow three Business Days to respond, with a reasonable extension where needed to obtain evidence or correct a notice failure.
6. Review available Seller, Platform and carrier records and the legally recoverable amount. Give a reasoned determination ordinarily within five Business Days after the response or response deadline.
7. A missing response is not an admission. Decide on the evidence and record the basis for Seller responsibility and amount.
8. Allow seven calendar days after the determination for internal appeal under Clause 26.5. A disputed assessment shall not be finally deducted until that appeal is decided; only a proportionate reserve under Clause 21.7 may remain pending.
9. Deduct only a lawfully finalized amount with an itemized statement. Reverse an incorrect assessment in the next practicable settlement or within seven Business Days of correction, whichever is earlier.
10. Internal finalization does not remove a Seller’s statutory remedy or a court’s authority to review the amount.

### 13.6 Calculation Example

Assume the delayed line has a tax-exclusive price of NPR 2,000 and a Seller-funded tax-exclusive discount of NPR 200. The Affected Product Value is NPR 1,800. Delivery of NPR 150 and a separately funded Platform promotion of NPR 100 do not change that base.

> **20% × NPR 1,800 = NPR 360 provisional assessment.**

The final recoverable amount may be lower or zero after review. For a tax-inclusive price, remove the applicable tax first; this example does not assume a tax rate for every Product.

### 13.7 Relationship to Other Losses

No duplicate recovery is permitted. The Clause 13 assessment is the ceiling for stipulated compensation for the same delay loss, subject to Applicable Law. Hasta Bazaar shall not bypass that ceiling by renaming the same loss as an administrative fee or indemnity. Distinct claims remain available only where legally recoverable, separately evidenced and non-duplicative; any overlap shall be credited.

### 13.8 Excluded Delay

The penalty does not apply to the extent delay is primarily caused by:

1. force majeure under Clause 32;
2. Hastabazaar’s system or operational error;
3. failure of an approved carrier to attend a confirmed pickup after the Seller timely recorded readiness and retained reasonable proof;
4. a Customer-requested or Customer-caused change or delay;
5. an Order modification or extension approved through the Platform;
6. a safety or compliance hold not caused by the Seller’s breach; or
7. another cause that Applicable Law prevents Hastabazaar from attributing to the Seller.

The Seller bears the burden of providing evidence reasonably within its possession, while Hastabazaar bears responsibility for checking Platform and carrier records within its control.

### 13.9 Additional Proportionate Measures

**Similarly, subject to the assessment safeguards and Applicable Law, a Seller-caused delay may, having regard to its seriousness, frequency, Customer impact, and the Seller’s response, result in one or more of the following proportionate measures:**

1. warning or corrective-action requirement;
2. Seller Performance-score adjustment;
3. reduced listing visibility under published performance criteria;
4. temporary order-volume limitation;
5. recovery of a distinct, legally recoverable loss only in accordance with Clause 13.7;
6. temporary suspension; or
7. termination for serious or repeated breach.

Any measure under items 3–7 is subject to Clause 26, except where urgent action is reasonably required for Customer safety, fraud, illegality, or regulatory compliance.

## 14. PACKAGING

### 14.1

The Seller shall package each Product according to its nature, fragility, size, weight, value, applicable safety requirements, and the Packaging Standards.

### 14.2

Any mandatory Hastabazaar-branded packaging programme and its cost shall be disclosed before it applies to the Seller.

### 14.3

The Seller is responsible for loss or damage primarily caused by inadequate or improper Seller packaging. Hastabazaar or the carrier shall retain and provide available evidence reasonably necessary to determine packaging responsibility.

## 15. DELIVERY, LOGISTICS, OWNERSHIP, AND RISK

### 15.1

Hastabazaar may engage approved third-party carriers. The Seller shall follow the applicable pickup, drop-off, tracking, proof-of-handover, and prohibited-carriage procedures.

### 15.2

Unless otherwise agreed, ownership remains with the Seller until it legally transfers to the Customer. Temporary possession by Hastabazaar or a carrier does not transfer ownership to Hastabazaar.

### 15.3

The Parties shall maintain appropriate proof of handover, including a scan, receipt, tracking event, photograph, or signed record.

### 15.4

Responsibility between Hastabazaar, the Seller, and a carrier for loss or damage shall be determined by packaging responsibility, proof and condition at handover, custody, declared-value requirements, insurance, the Logistics Policy, and Applicable Law.

### 15.5 Customer-Facing Remedy

Internal responsibility allocation shall not require the Customer to pursue a Seller or carrier where Applicable Law requires Hastabazaar to address the Customer’s complaint or remedy. Hastabazaar may provide the required Customer remedy first and recover the appropriate amount internally from the responsible Party or carrier.

### 15.6 Carrier-Fault Loss

If the Product was properly packaged, accurately declared, and documented as handed over to an approved carrier and is then lost or damaged primarily through carrier fault, Hastabazaar shall process or facilitate the Customer remedy and carrier claim. The Seller shall receive compensation, if applicable, according to the Logistics Policy, declared value, insurance limits, and Applicable Law.

## 16. CUSTOMER SERVICE AND GRIEVANCE MANAGEMENT

### 16.1

Hastabazaar shall maintain an electronic mechanism through which Customers can submit questions, complaints, reviews, ratings, and feedback.

### 16.2

Hastabazaar shall register a complaint upon receipt, immediately acknowledge it, and investigate, decide and communicate a reasoned written outcome within fifteen calendar days of receipt or a shorter mandatory period. Additional-information requests do not automatically suspend, restart or extend the deadline.

### 16.3

The Seller shall respond to a reasonable information or remedy request from Hastabazaar within forty-eight hours, or sooner where an urgent safety, fraud, legal, or perishable-Product issue reasonably requires action.

### 16.4

The Seller shall supply records, explanations, replacement availability, refund approval information, and other reasonable assistance. Seller delay shall not prevent Hastabazaar from meeting its Customer-facing legal obligations.

### 16.5

Repeated failure to cooperate may result in proportionate measures under Clause 26.

## 17. RETURNS, EXCHANGES, CANCELLATIONS, AND REFUNDS

### 17.1 Mandatory Rights

Nothing in this Agreement or a Platform Policy reduces a mandatory Customer right under Applicable Law. A Seller shall not display or enforce a blanket “No Return” or “No Refund” rule where prohibited by law.

### 17.2 Seller-Fault Return

The Seller shall bear the applicable refund, replacement, return, and reverse-logistics costs where the remedy results from:

1. wrong Product;
2. missing Product or component;
3. Product materially different from the listing or confirmed Order;
4. defective, unsafe, expired, or damaged Product attributable to the Seller;
5. counterfeit, illegal, or infringing Product;
6. false authenticity, origin, or handmade claim;
7. inadequate packaging;
8. failure to satisfy confirmed customization instructions;
9. Seller-caused delay giving rise to cancellation, return, or refund rights; or
10. another material Seller breach.

### 17.3 Logistics-Fault Return

Where loss or damage is primarily attributable to an approved carrier after proper packaging and documented handover, internal responsibility shall be determined under the Logistics Policy and Applicable Law without delaying a Customer remedy legally due.

### 17.4 Hastabazaar-Fault Return

Hastabazaar shall bear responsibility to the extent a return, cancellation, or loss is directly caused by Hastabazaar’s operational error.

### 17.5 Customer Return Without Seller Fault

Where a Customer lawfully exercises a return right without Seller-Fault, internal cost allocation shall follow Applicable Law and the Return, Exchange, Cancellation and Refund Policy, which must be disclosed before purchase.

### 17.6 Customized Products

A customized or personalized Product is not automatically excluded from return. Any restriction must be lawful, specifically disclosed before purchase, and shall not apply to a defect, unsafe Product, false description, or failure to follow confirmed requirements.

### 17.7 Refund Processing

Once a refund is approved or legally required, Hastabazaar shall initiate or complete it within seven days or any shorter period required by Applicable Law. Hastabazaar may recover the amount from the responsible Seller through settlement adjustment, reserve, or other lawful method after providing an itemized statement.

### 17.8 No Conditional Customer Remedy

A Customer refund legally due shall not be made conditional on Hastabazaar first recovering money from the Seller or carrier.

## 18. RETURNED PRODUCTS

### 18.1

The Seller shall accept a valid returned Product delivered to the registered return address unless a legitimate dispute is raised under this Clause.

### 18.2

The Seller may dispute the condition, identity, completeness, or handling of a returned Product within seven days after documented receipt. The dispute must include photographs, video, package condition, serial or batch information, and other reasonably available evidence.

### 18.3

Hastabazaar may investigate using listing records, Customer evidence, carrier records, unboxing material, and Seller evidence and shall provide a reasoned outcome.

### 18.4

If the Seller does not dispute within the stated period, the return record may be treated as accepted for settlement purposes, without limiting rights that cannot lawfully be waived.

### 18.5

If the Seller repeatedly refuses valid returns, Hastabazaar may arrange storage, redelivery, disposal, donation, or another lawful treatment only under a published procedure, after reasonable notice, and with an itemized allocation of reasonable costs.

## 19. WARRANTIES AND AFTER-SALES SUPPORT

### 19.1

The Seller shall honour every warranty, guarantee, repair, replacement, authenticity, and after-sales commitment stated in a listing, Product label, advertisement, or confirmed Order.

### 19.2

The Seller shall provide warranty instructions, required documentation, service location, turnaround time, exclusions, and contact details before purchase where applicable.

### 19.3

A warranty limitation does not exclude a mandatory statutory remedy.

## 20. MARKETPLACE FEES

### 20.1

Hastabazaar may charge only the fees clearly disclosed in the Seller Fee Schedule or separately accepted programme terms.

### 20.2

Fees may include Marketplace Commission, payment-processing charges where contractually applicable, logistics charges, reverse-logistics charges, optional photography or catalogue charges, storage charges, advertising charges, subscription fees, and other optional services expressly accepted by the Seller.

### 20.3

The Seller Fee Schedule shall state the amount or calculation method, tax treatment, event that triggers the fee, refund treatment, and effective date.

### 20.4

Hastabazaar shall not introduce a new material fee or increase a mandatory fee without the notice and acceptance process in Clause 29.

## 21. PAYMENTS, INVOICES, SETTLEMENTS, AND RESERVES

### 21.1 Customer Payments

Customer payments shall be processed through payment methods permitted by Applicable Law and, where required, a payment service or gateway approved by Nepal Rastra Bank.

### 21.2 Customer Invoice and Receipt

The Seller is responsible for the lawful tax invoice for the Product sale unless Applicable Law or an expressly documented invoicing arrangement assigns issuance to Hastabazaar on the Seller’s behalf. Hastabazaar shall ensure that the Customer receives the required electronic or physical invoice and payment receipt, including for cash payments where required.

### 21.3 Platform Fee Invoice

Hastabazaar shall provide the Seller with a lawful invoice or statement for commissions and services charged by Hastabazaar.

### 21.4 Settlement Cycle

Subject to this Agreement, Hastabazaar shall settle undisputed amounts within [●] Business Days after [successful delivery/expiry of the applicable return period/other agreed event]. The Seller Fee Schedule shall identify the settlement trigger and cycle.

### 21.5 Itemized Statement

Each settlement statement shall identify Orders, gross Product proceeds, Seller-funded discounts, Platform-funded promotions, taxes, commission, logistics charges, refunds, penalties, reserves, releases, and other adjustments.

### 21.6 Authorized Deductions

Hastabazaar may deduct only amounts authorized by this Agreement, accepted campaign terms, a final dispute decision, or Applicable Law, including fees, tax withholding, Customer refunds, chargebacks, the finalized Clause 13 penalty, and direct documented Seller liabilities.

### 21.7 Reserve or Hold

A hold requires documented grounds linked to identified refunds, chargebacks, suspected fraud, safety exposure, a binding legal requirement or probable Seller liability. Its amount shall be proportionate to the estimated exposure. Unless prohibited by law, notify the Seller of the grounds, transaction references, amount and next review date. Review at least every fifteen calendar days and promptly release amounts whose justification ends. No automatic rolling reserve applies unless its rate, duration and release mechanics are completed in Schedule 2 and separately accepted. A hold is not forfeiture or proof of debt; internal holds shall not delay Customer remedies.

### 21.8 Reconciliation Dispute

The Seller may dispute a settlement statement within [30] days after it becomes available. Hastabazaar shall investigate and provide a reasoned response. This internal period does not extinguish a right that cannot lawfully be limited.

### 21.9 No Improper Withholding

Undisputed amounts shall not be withheld merely because another amount is disputed, except for a proportionate reserve reasonably connected to the dispute.

## 22. TAXES AND RECORDS

### 22.1

The Seller is responsible for registration, filing, invoicing, and payment of taxes arising from its Product sales, except taxes legally imposed on Hastabazaar’s own income or services.

### 22.2

Hastabazaar may withhold and remit TDS or another amount when required by law and shall provide the available certificate or evidence.

### 22.3

Maintain transaction, invoice and supporting records for the applicable tax and other statutory retention periods. Before launch, approve a category-specific retention schedule with the accountant and legal adviser. Complaint and personal information shall not be retained indefinitely without a lawful need. A documented legal hold suspends deletion of relevant evidence only for as long as necessary and shall be periodically reviewed.

### 22.4

Neither Party provides tax advice to the other. Each Party should obtain its own professional advice.

## 23. PERSONAL INFORMATION, SECURITY, AND CONFIDENTIALITY

### 23.1 Customer Information

The Seller may access and use Customer personal information only as necessary to fulfil the Order, provide warranty or after-sales support, address a complaint, prevent fraud, or comply with law.

### 23.2 Prohibited Data Use

The Seller shall not sell Customer information, use it for unrelated marketing without valid consent, contact a Customer to bypass the Platform in relation to an Order, disclose it to an unauthorized person, or retain it longer than reasonably necessary or legally required.

### 23.3 Security

Each Party shall maintain reasonable technical, physical, and organizational safeguards. Sensitive authentication and identification information shall be protected using encryption or another legally required security measure.

### 23.4 Incident Notice

The Seller shall notify Hastabazaar without undue delay and, where practicable, within twenty-four hours after discovering unauthorized access, disclosure, loss, misuse, or compromise involving Platform or Customer information. The Seller shall cooperate in containment, investigation, notice, and remediation.

### 23.5 Confidential Information

Each Party shall protect non-public business, technical, financial, Seller, Customer, and operational information received from the other and use it only for this Agreement. This obligation does not apply to information lawfully public, independently developed, already lawfully known, or required to be disclosed by law.

### 23.6 Required Disclosure

Where legally permitted, a Party required to disclose confidential information shall give the other Party reasonable advance notice and disclose only what is legally required.

### 23.7 Survival

Confidentiality and lawful data-use obligations survive termination for as long as the information remains protected by law or its confidential nature.

## 24. RATINGS, REVIEWS, AND FAIR CONDUCT

### 24.1

The Seller shall not, directly or through an employee, family member, affiliate, agent, paid reviewer, or false Customer account:

1. review or rate its own Products;
2. submit fabricated feedback;
3. manipulate ratings or suppress legitimate complaints;
4. threaten, reward, or improperly pressure a Customer concerning a review; or
5. engage in another unfair commercial practice.

### 24.2

The Seller may request honest reviews using Platform-approved tools. No reward or other benefit may be conditioned on a positive review. Any lawful incentive for an honest review must be transparently disclosed.

### 24.3

Hastabazaar may moderate content for fraud, abuse, irrelevance, illegality, conflicts of interest, or policy violations but shall not remove genuine negative feedback merely because it is unfavorable.

## 25. INTELLECTUAL PROPERTY

### 25.1 Seller Content

The Seller retains ownership of its original photographs, videos, descriptions, trademarks, designs, and other listing content (**“Seller Content”**).

### 25.2 Licence

The Seller grants Hastabazaar a non-exclusive, royalty-free, transferable to service providers, sublicensable, and geographically unrestricted licence during the Agreement to host, reproduce, format, translate, display, distribute, and promote Seller Content for Platform operation and marketing. After termination, Hastabazaar may retain archival copies for legal, accounting, dispute, and security purposes but shall cease new promotional use within a reasonable period.

### 25.3 Third-Party Content

The Seller shall not upload content it lacks authority to use. Hastabazaar may remove content upon a credible infringement notice and may request evidence, notify the Seller, and restore content where a complaint is withdrawn or shown to be unfounded.

### 25.4 Platform Rights

Hastabazaar owns or lawfully uses its Platform software, branding, templates, marketplace data, badge designs, and other Platform materials. No ownership transfers to the Seller.

### 25.5 Seller Data

Nothing in this Clause transfers ownership of the Seller’s underlying business records. Hastabazaar may use aggregated or appropriately de-identified marketplace information for analytics, security, service improvement, and lawful business planning.

## 26. SELLER PERFORMANCE, CORRECTIVE ACTION, AND SUSPENSION

### 26.1 Objective Factors

Seller Performance may consider fulfilment timeliness, cancellation, valid complaints, Product conformity, authenticity, return rate attributable to Seller-Fault, response time, packaging, policy compliance, and fraud or safety risk.

### 26.2 Ordinary Procedure

Except for urgent action under Clause 26.3, Hastabazaar shall provide notice of the issue, available supporting information, the proposed measure, and at least [7] days to respond or cure where cure is reasonably possible.

### 26.3 Immediate Action

Hastabazaar may immediately restrict a listing, Order, payment, or Seller Account where reasonably necessary because of suspected fraud, counterfeit or illegal Products, urgent safety risk, unauthorized access, regulatory instruction, evidence preservation, material data breach, or probable serious Customer harm.

### 26.4 Proportionality

Measures may include warning, training, correction, listing removal, badge removal, visibility reduction, order-volume limitation, reserve, temporary suspension, or termination. Hastabazaar shall select a measure proportionate to severity, recurrence, Customer impact, Seller cooperation, and legal risk.

### 26.5 Appeal

The Seller may appeal within seven days after notice of a final measure, with supporting evidence. Hastabazaar shall issue a reasoned internal appeal decision ordinarily within fifteen days. An appeal does not automatically stay an urgent safety, fraud, or legal restriction.

### 26.6 Pending Amounts

Suspension does not forfeit earned, undisputed Settlement Amounts. Hastabazaar may retain only a proportionate hold authorized by Clause 21.7 or Applicable Law.

## 27. AUDIT, INSPECTION, AND COOPERATION

### 27.1

On reasonable notice, Hastabazaar may request records or conduct a proportionate inspection relevant to registration, authenticity, safety, tax invoices, inventory, sourcing, Product quality, complaints, or compliance.

### 27.2

Advance notice may be omitted where a proportionate urgent records request is necessary for suspected fraud, imminent safety risk, evidence preservation or lawful authority requirements. This does not authorize trespass, forced entry, unauthorized device access or seizure. Physical access requires valid consent or lawful authority.

### 27.3

Hastabazaar shall minimize operational disruption and protect confidential information obtained during an audit.

### 27.4

The Seller shall cooperate with lawful requests from Hastabazaar, regulators, inspection officers, courts, payment providers, and carriers relating to transactions within scope.

## 28. INDEMNITY AND LIABILITY

### 28.1 Seller Indemnity

Subject to Clauses 28.2–28.3 and Applicable Law, the Seller shall indemnify Hasta Bazaar for reasonable, documented direct losses, legally payable Customer compensation, third-party claims and reasonable defence costs attributable to:

1. unlawful, unsafe, defective, counterfeit or infringing Products;
2. false listing, authenticity or origin claims;
3. Seller tax, invoicing, licence or regulatory breach;
4. Seller-attributable packaging or fulfilment failures;
5. unauthorized Customer-data use or disclosure;
6. breach of Seller warranties; or
7. Seller fraud, wilful misconduct or negligence.

This does not transfer criminal responsibility or any fine, penalty or liability that the law prohibits shifting, and does not exempt Hasta Bazaar from duties owed to Customers or authorities.

### 28.2 Exclusions

The Seller is not responsible to the extent a claim results from Hastabazaar’s or a carrier’s own breach, negligence, unauthorized listing change, system error, or unlawful conduct.

### 28.3 Claims Procedure

Provide reasonably prompt notice, the grounds and available evidence; permit a reasonable response and participation in defence; and mitigate loss. Neither Party shall make an admission or settlement imposing liability or a non-monetary obligation on the other without written consent. A disputed amount shall not become recoverable merely because it was demanded; apply the contractual dispute procedure and Applicable Law. No duplicate recovery is permitted, and Clause 13.7 governs overlap with delay compensation. Late notice reduces liability only to the extent of actual prejudice.

### 28.4 Direct Loss

Except for liabilities that cannot lawfully be limited, neither Party is liable to the other for remote, speculative, or purely indirect loss not reasonably arising from the breach.

### 28.5 Liability Cap

No monetary liability cap is activated by a blank or incomplete schedule. A negotiated business-to-business cap requires a completed written addendum and express acceptance before it applies prospectively. It must preserve unpaid settlements, legally due refunds, fraud, wilful misconduct, gross negligence, Product-safety obligations and other liabilities that cannot lawfully be limited. This Agreement does not purport to exclude liability merely because an independent Seller or carrier is involved.

### 28.6 Mandatory Rights

Nothing in this Agreement limits Customer rights or regulatory liabilities that cannot lawfully be excluded or limited.

